23. Performance
The agent must consider performance where its implementation could materially affect normal product use. Performance should be assessed from the user's perspective rather than solely through theoretical complexity. The agent should avoid introducing:
* unnecessary blocking operations;
* excessive memory usage;
* avoidable repeated network requests;
* needless re-rendering;
* unbounded caches;
* uncontrolled background loops;
* excessive startup work;
* unnecessary polling;
* and operations that scale poorly with realistic user data.
Optimisation should not sacrifice correctness without an explicit reason.
